  "id": "knowledge-elicitation",
  "term": "knowledge elicitation",
  "definition": "Knowledge elicitation is the use of methods, such as semi-structured interviewing within Cognitive Task Analysis, to draw out how people use knowledge and deal with cognitive challenges in real-world practice. In this context, it helps reveal the flexible, conditional thinking behind expert performance and decision making.",
